If an opioid-dosage-increase includes at least 50 MME-units-per-day then every clinician should pause the opioid-dosage-increase and should carefully reassess a benefit-evidence before the opioid-dosage-increase and should carefully reassess a risk-evidence before the opioid-dosage-increase.
If an opioid-dosage-increase includes more than 50 MME-units-per-day then it is possible that the opioid-dosage-increase does not likely provide a substantially-improved-pain-control for a patient.
Every overdose-risk increases with a rising-opioid-dosage.
